{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01FBM2BDu29GFZpFvUVGK9n2","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Anchor is a self-contained personal productivity + R&D mission-control system for J.C. Liechty. Grounded claims:\n\n- **It's a single-folder, local-first productivity system** living entirely in `C:\\dev\\Anchor` (no OneDrive/sync), with **plain markdown as the source of truth** (`DASHBOARD.md`, `PROJECTS.md`, `INBOX.md`, domain files under `domains/`, plus daily `logs/`). No database, no binary formats.\n\n- **It ships a standalone web-app dashboard** (`anchor_gui.py`) â€” a Python stdlib-only HTTP server bound to `http://localhost:8777`, run persistently as the NSSM Windows service `anchor`. The browser UI is fully interactive: check off tasks, add tasks, capture ideas, edit/cancel/save/restore â€” all writing straight back to the markdown files. A CLI mirror (`anchor.py`) provides the same operations and generates a static `dashboard.html`.\n\n- **It models a full task lifecycle** â€” Active â†’ Done â†’ Cancelled â†’ Saved-for-Later â†’ Restored â€” across life domains (academic, commercial, family, writing), with priority/energy/due/notes metadata per task.\n\n- **It has grown a substantial \"R&D Control Surface\"** that turns each project into a cockpit for \"trio\"-driven development (the researchPrime â†’ Crucible â†’ Foreman skill trio). This is the bulk of recent engineering, built in four design waves (v2â€“v4, all merged to master):\n  - **v2** added the session model, cached/validated AI summaries, a Grass-Catchers idea lane, deliverable pin/declare, and an interactive terminal substrate.\n  - **v3 \"Mission Control\"** added real ConPTY terminals (the one declared native dependency, optional `pywinpty`), per-session git-worktree isolation, a stacking window manager, in-place cached summaries, stage handoffs, runnable deliverable previews (always on a port â‰  8777), and Ghost World Labs branding.\n  - **v4 \"Project Cockpit\"** (current, merged commit `38fd70e`, 637 tests passing) added: one terminal substrate that auto-loads the lane's skill **once** and greets once (killing a repeating-prompt bug), a Claudeâ†”Gemini engine toggle with per-project persistence, Paradigm-2 inline expanding lane panels with status lights, per-lane doc-roles, a cost/tokens/time rollup, grass-idea promotion, and type-aware deliverable launch.\n\n- **It is self-testing**: `anchor_healthcheck.py` runs every morning at 5 AM via Task Scheduler, parsing every markdown file, exercising every HTTP endpoint on a throwaway port, and walking the v2/v3/v4 R&D surfaces fully stubbed (no live `claude`, never touching `:8777`); failures surface as a red dashboard banner.\n\nIn short: **a personal markdown-backed task/project manager that has evolved into a local mission-control dashboard for orchestrating AI-driven R&D projects.**"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4410,"cache_read_input_tokens":45292,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4410,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"91a3c31b-7e7c-45e0-9206-f26f693a7c36","uuid":"bbedf9df-9b0b-49ba-a048-8c4d5c9e7e44","request_id":"req_011Cc1JPD65HumW1KgriGLC4"}
